+# Title
+
+Open data pipeline: batch sources, SSE consumer, dbt star schema and marts (gh-1)
+
+# Body
+
+## Summary
+
+- Batch sources (sitematrix, Census 2024 county population, USAspending FY2024 prime awards) load to Parquet under `lake/raw/`. `make build` runs them, then `dbt build`.
+- `make stream DURATION=<s>` consumes the Wikimedia recentchange replay over SSE. It resumes from a persisted cursor, dedupes on `meta.id`, and sets the late flag at first arrival.
+- dbt-duckdb staging and star schema, with contracts and key tests. Publishes four marts to `out/marts/`.
+- `oracle_map.yml` with seven checks (`python -m pipeline.oracle`). All seven pass on the run recorded in `outputs/summary.md`.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+- Question A covers agencies 417, 418, 474 and 485 only.
+- Most FY2024 award rows (79%) have no county reported. Their totals sit in state-unallocated rows.
+- The stream is a replay. Canary events and one truncated replay frame are not stored.
+
+## Decisions
+
+See `DECISIONS.md`, including the replay-server probe (the server replays from `Last-Event-ID`) and the population vintage (July 1, 2024).
+
+## Test plan
+
+- `uv sync --locked`
+- `uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` (46 tests)
+- `make build` (exit 0 on a clean checkout; a second run leaves the marts unchanged)
+- `make stream DURATION=60` (exit 0)
+- `uv run python -m pipeline.oracle run` (checks 1 to 6)
+- `uv run python -m pipeline.oracle run --check resume_equivalence` (check 7)
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
