+# Open data pipeline (gh-1), summary
+
+## What was built
+
+- `make build`: loads three batch sources to `lake/raw/` (sitematrix, Census 2024 county population, USAspending FY2024 prime awards), writes an empty stream store if none exists, then runs `dbt build` (staging, star schema, marts, singular tests).
+- `make stream DURATION=<s>`: consumes the Wikimedia recentchange replay over SSE. It resumes from a persisted cursor and dedupes on `meta.id`. The late flag is set at first arrival and stored.
+- Marts in `out/marts/`: `mart_obligations_by_geo_agency_month`, `mart_obligations_by_state_month`, `fct_wiki_edit_5min`, `late_events`.
+- `oracle_map.yml` with seven checks, run by `python -m pipeline.oracle`.
+
+## Oracle results
+
+Run after `make build` from a clean state, with a 60-second stream.
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| 1 raw_row_conservation | pass: 9,820 distinct FY2024 rows = recorded per-zip count |
+| 2 obligation_total_exact | pass: 1,442,017,216.67 from the marts = independent CSV sum (9,820 rows) |
+| 3 state_equals_county | pass: 0 state-month keys differ |
+| 4 per_person_recompute | pass: 2,724 rows, 0 mismatches (Decimal recompute, half-up) |
+| 5 stream_no_duplicate_ids | pass: 21,500 rows = 21,500 distinct `meta_id` |
+| 6 window_conservation | pass: 21,441 edits in windows + 59 late events = 21,500 stored events |
+| 7 resume_equivalence | pass: a consumer killed and restarted stores the same 2,000 arrival-ordered rows as an uninterrupted run |
+
+Idempotence: two consecutive `make build` runs give identical row counts and sorted-row hashes for all four marts.
+
+Data-quality checks: singular tests confirm the staged FY2024 total and row count match an independent read of the zip CSVs (`zipfs`), and that no obligation value has more than two decimals. `dbt build` reports 74 of 74 passing.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Question A covers agencies 417, 418, 474 and 485 only (USAspending archive scope). Totals are not all federal obligations.
+- County is reported for only 21% of FY2024 rows (2,039 of 9,820 by count, about $0.39B of $1.44B). The rest sit in state-unallocated keys ("(county not reported)") and are shown in the state rollup. Per-county figures understate the true county totals.
+- 32 mart rows (39 awards, $7.2M) carry a county FIPS that the 2024 Census county file does not contain (territories and Connecticut 09xxx). Their population is null, so per-person values are null.
+- Per-person values exist only for the 1,214 census-county rows.
+- The stream is a replay, not a live feed. Two canary events are not stored (Wikimedia test traffic). One replay frame is truncated inside its JSON and cannot be parsed; it is not stored.
+- Replay server resume: the server replays from `Last-Event-ID`, inclusive. The restart test killed the consumer, not the replay server.
+- Oracle check 7 is not run by `make build` or `make stream`. It runs as `python -m pipeline.oracle run --check resume_equivalence`.
