+# Pipeline
+
+## Stream probe (Phase 3, MF-1 mode)
+
+Probed 2026-10-22 against `http://localhost:8099/v2/stream/recentchange`.
+
+- Event fields: `meta` (`id`, `dt`, `uri`, `topic`, `partition`, `offset`, ...), `type`, `namespace`, `title`, `bot`, `wiki`, `length` (`old`, `new`), `user`, `timestamp`.
+- `id:` line format: a JSON array of topic and partition positions, for example `[{"topic":"eqiad.mediawiki.recentchange","partition":0,"timestamp":...},{"topic":"codfw.mediawiki.recentchange","partition":0,"offset":-1}]`.
+- The `id:` value is not unique per event. In a 5-second capture, 1921 events carried 1311 distinct `id:` values. `meta.id` is unique per event.
+- Reconnect with `Last-Event-ID`: the server replays from the event that carries that id, inclusive. The first events after reconnect were the events at positions 1, 2, 3 of the first capture, so the server honors the header.
+
+Mode: **R** (the server replays from `Last-Event-ID`). Dedupe on `meta.id` covers the replay. S2 is tested as written.
+
+## Consumer
+
+- `pipeline/stream.py`: SSE parsing, window bounds, the late rule (`LATE_AFTER`, `is_late`) and the commit of rows and cursor.
+- Stored rows: `lake/raw/stream_events/part-*.parquet`. The cursor is `lake/state/cursor.json` (last `id:` value only). Disconnects are recorded in `lake/state/gaps.json`.
+- Startup reloads the seen `meta_id` set, the running max `meta_dt` and the next `arrival_seq` from the stored rows.
+- Run: `make stream DURATION=<seconds>`.
+
+## Stream frames that are not stored
+
+- Canary events (`meta.domain` = `canary`) are Wikimedia test traffic with no wiki or namespace. They are counted as `canary` and not stored.
+- The replay sends one truncated `data:` frame (event `a0f69b5d-0c87-48d0-bbe5-c07b7c8c0262`, cut off inside the JSON after about 440 characters). It cannot be parsed. It is counted as `malformed` and not stored. This is a known limit of the replay server.
